==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|softely}}, {{m|enm|softeliche}}, equivalent to {{suffix|en|soft|ly|nocat=1}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈsɔftli/|a=GA}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈsɑftli/|a=cot-caught}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈsɒftli/|a=RP}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-softly.ogg|a=US}}

===Adverb===
{{en-adv|er|more}}

# In a [[soft]] manner; [[gently]].
#: {{ux|en|The masseuse was rubbing my back too '''softly''' for my liking, so I asked her to go harder.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1861|author=Anthony Trollope|title=Framley Parsonage
|passage=He had married a lady well educated and '''softly''' nurtured, but not dowered with worldly wealth. {{...}} They would give up ideas of gentle living, of soft raiment, and delicate feeding.}}
# Not [[loudly]]; nearly [[inaudible|inaudibly]].
#: {{ux|en|whisper '''softly''' in someone's ear}}
#: {{ux|en|play music '''softly'''}}

